Z||000000||BBBAD GT||02-22-2000||02:38 PM||||I've had my 87 GT for 3 weeks now, and more than half of the people that see me with it says "Is that your new 'Toy'"?  I'm guessing they say that because I'm always into cars, or from that fact that I WAS driving a 4 door Mercury Tracer (its for sale, BTW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) Anyway, anybody else hear that from people who see you in your Fiero for the first time?  I now have too much respect for the Fiero to say "yeah..new toy".   <P>BTW, I love the GT.  I drive it everyday, without any problems to speak of.  Replaced the cap/rotor/wires/plugs/pcv/fuel filter over the weekend, and it runs better now than it ever did (had no problems before).  I'm amazed it was running as good as it did with all the stock old stuff I replaced at 85k miles.  <P> <A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Reality||02-22-2000||03:10 PM||||I have some dealings with people and their cars and car clubs and most of them when they are referring to anyone who decides to venture down the path of getting a new car, always call the new car a "Toy" just because of the saying boyz and their toyz. I don't know weird little thing guys like to do I guess.||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||02-22-2000||05:19 PM||||The "boys and their toys" comments are usually reserved for non-essential things like boats, ATVs, <B>sports</B> cars, etc...<BR>In this light, having your Fiero refered to as a toy is good. It means they recognize it as something other that just everyday transportation!<BR>||||reg||14
